START

1. Define the production function:
       f(x) = x × (10 - x)

2. Set GA parameters:
       Population size = 10
       Mutation rate = 0.1
       Crossover rate = 0.8
       Number of generations = 20
       Resource range = 0 to 10

3. Create an initial population
       Generate 10 random resource values between 0 and 10

4. Calculate fitness
       Fitness = f(x)

5. Repeat for each generation:

       a. Select two parents
          Choose the better individuals based on fitness

       b. Perform crossover
          Combine the two parents to create children

       c. Perform mutation
          Randomly change the children's resource values

       d. Keep values within 0 to 10

       e. Create the new population

       f. Find the best solution
          Select the individual with maximum fitness

       g. Display:
          Generation
          Best solution
          Fitness

6. After all generations:
       Display the final best resource allocation
       Display the maximum production

STOP
